   "text": {
    "L1": "A face is flat. An edge is where two faces meet, and a corner is where edges meet.",
    "L2": "Here is a common mistake: count only the faces visible in the picture. That misses hidden faces.",
    "L3": "Count a solid in pairs: top and bottom, front and back, left and right.",
    "L4": "So a cube has six faces, even when a picture shows only some of them.",
    "L5": "For edges, count four around the top, four around the bottom, and four standing up. That makes twelve.",
    "L6": "For corners, count four on top and four at the bottom. That makes eight.",
    "L7": "A cuboid may have faces of different sizes, but it still has six faces, twelve edges and eight corners.",
    "L8": "Now check your understanding: choose the complete count for a cube."
   },
